          "back": "- [4...Nxe5 5.d4] is the most common. We restore material equality and gain some advantage, but there are a few traps to avoid.\n- 4...Bxf2+?! is dubious but leads to fun complications. Black returns the piece and thus avoids the fork trick.\n- [4...Nf6 5.Nxc6 dxc6 6.h3]: White is much better, as Black has no compensation for the pawn.\n- [4...Qh4 5.g3] or [4...Qf6 5.Ng4] are easily defused attempts at a Scholar's Mate."
